    "attempt": 1,
    "rationale": "I translated these from /src/infra/app.tf and /src/chart/values.yaml. The evidence is incomplete, so risk is high. inventory_describe returned analysis status 'unconfigured', every control row in controls_describe is UNKNOWN for both src and dst, and platform_state.evidence is empty, so I cite no evidence ids. What I translated: (1) The chat_app IAM role became a namespaced Role and RoleBinding in namespace 'chat' for ServiceAccount chat-app (automount off). It can only 'get' two named Secrets and cannot list or watch, and there are no cluster-scoped roles or wildcards. On-prem the app reads its password from a mounted Secret (passwordSource env-file), so it needs no Secrets Manager or KMS API rights. (2) The strong attachments bucket policy became an RGW bucket policy. It has an explicit Deny for non-TLS requests. Allows go only to the RGW user chat-app: s3:ListBucket on the bucket, and s3:GetObject and s3:PutObject on objects. These are the same actions as the source role, and Delete is not granted. The Deny-insecure statement uses a '*' principal only in a Deny, as the source does, and no Allow has a wildcard principal. I did not translate the demo_weak_bucket_policy variant (s3:* for the account root). The bucket name 'chat-attachments' and RGW user ARN are placeholders, because the source uses bucket_prefix and the RGW tenant/user is not in inventory. (3) The external_secrets IAM role became an OpenBao policy, narrowed from the source's '<name>/*' prefix read to two exact paths. It can read and push (create/update) only to db-app, and read chat-admin. List is not granted. (4) The db_app Secrets Manager secret became an ExternalSecret that uses a namespaced SecretStore, not a ClusterSecretStore. Not translated: the KMS CMK and its key policy (S3 SSE-KMS / customer key), aws:kms:ViaService scoping, and S3 versioning/recovery window. There is no target-format type for these in this step. I checked the proposal with policy_evaluate and it came back valid with no problems.",
    "risk": "high",
