    "exception_justifications": [
      {
        "control_id": "AUD-01",
        "justification": "None of these translations sets up audit logging. On the source, CloudTrail/S3 access logging is not shown in app.tf. On the destination, the OpenBao audit device, Kubernetes API audit policy and RGW ops log are platform-level settings outside this scope. The approver must confirm them separately. Both src and dst are UNKNOWN."
      },
      {
        "control_id": "NET-01",
        "justification": "In chart values, networkPolicy.enabled is false and ingress/egress are empty, so these policy translations do not give default deny. The network role must add namespace default-deny plus allow rules for the edge, PgBouncer, RGW, OTel and DNS. Until then NET-01 is an open gap."
      },
      {
        "control_id": "DR-01",
        "justification": "Source S3 versioning (Enabled) and a Secrets Manager recovery window of 0 days (demo setting) are not represented in any target format here. No backup, or restore into a new environment, has been shown. Destination RGW bucket versioning and OpenBao snapshot/restore need separate evidence."
      },
      {
        "control_id": "ENC-02",
        "justification": "Source at-rest encryption uses a customer KMS CMK (SSE-KMS with bucket key, and a Secrets Manager kms_key_id) with rotation enabled. This translation has no format for an RGW SSE-KMS key (e.g. via OpenBao transit) or for OpenBao storage-barrier key settings. Customer-key equivalence on the destination is unverified, which also affects the 'customer key' part of SEC-01."
      }
    ],
    "audit_summary": "Plan p-aedeef1f-a338-4279-8c14-3ec7f4bb56b4 translates AWS policies to on-prem formats in 4 translations:\n1. IAM role chat_app → namespaced k8s RBAC in 'chat'. It can only get two named Secrets: no list or watch, no cluster scope, no wildcards.\n2. S3 attachments bucket policy (strong variant) → RGW bucket policy. Non-TLS requests are denied. Only the chat-app user can List/Get/Put; Delete is not granted.\n3. IAM role external_secrets → OpenBao policy, narrowed from a prefix wildcard to exact paths, with no list.\n4. Secrets Manager db_app → ExternalSecret using a namespaced SecretStore.\n\nMapped controls: IAM-01, SEC-01, ISO-01, ENC-01, ENC-02.\n\nOpen gaps, each with an exception justification: AUD-01, NET-01, DR-01, and ENC-02 (customer-key equivalence).\n\nThere is no evidence: inventory analysis is unconfigured and all control results are UNKNOWN. Risk is high.\n\nBefore approving, the approver should confirm:\n- the real bucket name and RGW user ARN (both placeholders here)\n- the OpenBao mount path 'secret/' and env 'onprem'\n- that the weak demo bucket policy is not the one in force at the source\n\nThis proposal does not decide any control or gate verdict."
